  "source_text": "A turquoise horse earring is one of the unrecovered belongings listed by the FBI in Amy Mihaljevic’s case.\n\nAmy was ten when she was abducted from a shopping center in Bay Village, Ohio, on October 27, 1989. A jogger found her body in rural Ashland County on February 8, 1990.\n\nThe FBI says three items believed to have been with Amy were never recovered: that earring, black ankle boots and a black leather binder.\n\nThose details are part of a public request for information. They do not establish what happened to the objects or identify the person responsible.\n",
  "duration_seconds": 41.65659863945578,
